# Commit before redeploy

If you are about to tell the user to redeploy Coolify (or any production deploy):

1. Commit the relevant work in this repo.
2. Push to GitHub (`origin`) so the commit exists on the remote.
3. Only then say “redeploy.”

Do not ask the user to redeploy uncommitted or unpushed work. Do not commit secrets. Do not push `--force` to main. If a main push looks risky, use a branch + PR instead.

This is an exception to “only commit when asked”: a redeploy request counts as asking to publish the work.

Keep `ai-office-backend` in its own repo. Do not commit or push backend files here.
